  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A man named Timothy Taylor is said to have brought a piece of metal from the 1947 Roswell crash, a wreck in New Mexico that some say was a craft from elsewhere, and placed it in the hands of North Carolina man Chris Bledsoe and his family. Bob McGwier, a CIA contractor, tells it as something he heard, and Michels adds that Bledsoe somehow knew the material was not from here. Bledsoe himself tells it as a test of his family by a man from NASA, the US space agency, who arrived with a backpack and credentials covering \"everything from Area 51 to the CIA\", without saying the metal came from Roswell."
}
